@startuml
' Source of truth for: assets/diagrams/learning/data-plane/ngfw/snort-verdict-roundtrip.svg
' Re-render with: plantuml -tsvg snort-verdict-roundtrip.puml
title How a Verdict Gets Back to VPP\n(patched Snort -> thread-local storage -> DAQ copies to shared descriptor)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

start
:1 · VPP enqueues the packet\nwrites a descriptor (offset into buffer pool), bumps the enqueue head; #f0fdfa
:2 · Snort DAQ dequeues it\nreads the descriptor, resolves the offset, presents the packet to Snort; #fff1f2
:3 · Snort evaluates rules — on a match, fpLogEvent() fires\nwrites THREAD-LOCAL storage (not a log file):\nsnort_sid_entries[] (SID+verdict) · snort_sid_count · snort_detected_appid; #fff1f2
:4 · AppID event (optional)\nAppIdVppHandler catches the DataBus event, updates thread-local AppID; #fff1f2
:5 · daq_vpp_msg_finalize() — the hand-off (star)\nreads thread-local SID/verdict/AppID and COPIES them into the descriptor\nmetadata union (verdict + appid + sid_entries[10]); resets Snort's counters; #fffbeb
:6 · Snort signals VPP\natomically bumps the dequeue head, wakes VPP via deq_fd eventfd (or VPP polls); #fff1f2
:7 · VPP dequeue node reads the verdict\nPASS -> continue the feature arc (to ngfw-post-snort)\nBLOCK -> error-drop; VPP tallies verdict / SID / AppID counters; #f0fdfa
stop

note right
No log parsing, no sockets on the hot path —
just a shared-memory descriptor + one eventfd wake.
If Snort dies, the instance's on-disconnect policy
(drop | pass) decides what VPP does with new packets.
end note
@enduml
